Found under k293 (2026-10-31). lib/OCP/Cmd/Destroy.pm (~line 515) prints "Are you sure you want to destroy this cluster? [y/N] " on STDOUT and reads <STDIN> with no terminal check. So a piped `y` (a here-string, `yes |`, a CI step) confirms deleting real servers. Since k293, `ocp node trust-host` refuses a non-terminal confirmation and points at `--yes`, following ADR 0030. destroy has `--force` for the same job.

Done =
- without a terminal, destroy does not read STDIN: it says on STDERR that it needs a terminal or `--force`, and exits 1 with nothing deleted;
- the prompt goes to STDERR (a prompt is not payload), like TrustHost;
- the same for the per-node candidate prompt (POD around line 934), if it has its own read;
- tests for piped y, closed STDIN, and a terminal stand-in (TrustHost uses an `_interactive` attribute for that);
- a Changes bullet, since scripts that piped `y` now need `--force`.

